SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ggeettccoonntteexxtt() and sseettccoonntteexxtt() functions conform to X/Open System
     Interfaces and Headers Issue 5 (“XSH5”) and IEEE Std 1003.1-2001
     (“POSIX.1”).  The _e_r_r_n_o indications are an extension to the standard.

     The IEEE Std 1003.1-2004 (“POSIX.1”) revision marked the functions
     ggeettccoonntteexxtt() and sseettccoonntteexxtt() as obsolete, citing portability issues and
     recommending the use of POSIX threads instead.  The IEEE Std 1003.1-2008
     (“POSIX.1”) revision removed the functions from the specification.

